+pve-firewall (6.0.6+supermox2) trixie; urgency=medium
+
+  * debian: init.d/pve-firewall no longer pins the iptables family to the legacy
+    backend. SuperMox kernels carry no legacy ebtables bridge module, so the
+    pin made every pve-firewall status update fail with
+    "modprobe: FATAL: Module ebtables not found" once every 10 seconds; the
+    nft backend Debian selects by default is the one that works.
+
+ -- SuperMox <noreply@supermox.me>  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 02:18:46 -0800
+
 pve-firewall (6.0.6) trixie; urgency=medium
 
   * rules: read protocols, services and ethertypes from the new
